+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Our services need to change JSON documents with standard patches. The library already implements JSON Pointer (RFC 6901); JSON Patch (RFC 6902) builds directly on it and is the published standard for expressing document updates.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 6902 with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- The function returns the patched document as a new value and never mutates its input (nor the patch).
+- It throws when the patch is malformed or when any operation fails; no partial result is returned.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- New code in `src/` (re-exported from `src/index.ts`) and new tests in `test/`.
+- No new dependencies. The existing `json-pointer` behaviour is unchanged.
